    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left knee pain, patient-reported"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left anterior/medial knee ache, described as 'like bruise under kneecap'; began approximately 2–3 weeks ago after lifting boxes and a big weekend. Pain 3–4/10 at baseline, up to 6/10 on stairs, especially going down. Worse with stairs, squatting, and getting up from a chair after prolonged sitting; settles with rest. No night pain or significant morning stiffness over 10 minutes. No clear trauma, true locking, giving way, or catching. Unsure about swelling, described as 'maybe puffy evenings'. Fully weight-bearing and mobilising unaided. No previous similar symptoms."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neck pain, patient-reported"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Central/right paracervical ache described as 'tight muscles' for approximately 6 weeks, with occasional brief sharp twinge on sudden turning. Worse with prolonged desk work, looking down at phone, and driving; better with heat, stretching, ibuprofen, and lying down. No arm pain, paraesthesia, weakness, clumsiness, gait change, bowel or bladder symptoms, or trauma. Sleep a bit disturbed by waking to change position."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood, patient-reported"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Described mood as 'a bit cranky'; denies low mood, anhedonia, and anxiety."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance and behaviour"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well, no acute distress; talkative and tangential, needed refocusing several times."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neck examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Normal alignment; no deformity. Increased tone and tenderness in upper trapezius and paracervical muscles, right greater than left. No midline cervical spine tenderness. Rotation mildly reduced bilaterally with pain at end range; flexion and extension near full."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Upper limb neurological and related examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Upper limb power 5/5 in all myotomes; light-touch sensation intact; biceps, triceps, and brachioradialis reflexes 2+ and symmetrical. Spurling test negative. Gait normal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left knee examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No obvious swelling, erythema, or deformity; no effusion. Mild tenderness at the medial patellar margin and medial patellofemoral joint. Full range of motion with mild anterior pain on deep flexion. McMurray test negative; ligaments stable to varus and valgus stress. Patellar grind reproduces symptoms. Normal gait; able to partial squat with anterior knee pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
